cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Draft 00, non-normative. Cite it as a draft, not as a standard."
title: "UIBC: Unified Integrity Boundary Check — specification, draft 00"
abstract: >-
  A portable package binds an agent's identity, lifecycle events and action
  evidence into one hash-committed structure, and a verification procedure
  returns one of three outcomes - PASS, FAIL, or the explicit UNKNOWN - from
  bytes alone. The draft names what cannot be checked from those bytes, and it
  states the boundary of unpinned verification: a package re-sealed by another
  key verifies against itself, so authorship requires pinning.
type: report
authors:
